    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68593" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονο-μερής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>consisting of one part, single</i>, opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυμερής, φιλοσοφία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					7.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>for one side</i>, of a bandage, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				794
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ μ.</span>
			<i>after hearing only one side</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cal.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μ.</span>
			<i>ex parte</i> applications, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mag.</u>
				3.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. μαρτυρίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Just.
					<u>Nov.</u>
					90.9
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μερῶς</span>
			<i>in a one-sided manner</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				136.2
			</span></i>.</div>
